§ feedback / rqmts

☑ search — the $.field query language now works in the TABLE, not just the
  inspector: a field query annotates rather than hides, driving the match counts
  below. Plain-text still filters connections by URL.
☑ aggregation — bandwidth is the default per-node aggregate (↑/↓ on ALL + every
  process/container header); the agg button / m toggles bandwidth ⇄ message
  count. (controls.aggMetric, components/agg.jsx)
☑ error detection — done via SEARCH as suggested, not a bespoke feature: a
  $.field query (e.g. $.error) turns the per-node aggregate into matching / total
  messages, live, flagged red when >0 — per service AND per connection row. So
  "show error per service" = type $.error and watch the counts.

¶ These are ecs services btw (relevant to the egress-cost concern above).

☑ hardcoded support for standard binaries — no --bin/--pid now auto-discovers a
  running node/deno/bun/python/ruby and traces its SSL binary; --bin is only for
  extras. (probes/probe.js knownRuntimeBin / KNOWN_BINS)

